      "texts": {
        "at-0001": "Round money only with round_money Always round monetary results with ledgerly.money.round_money (half-up to the cent); never use Python's round() or a bare Decimal.quantize(), which use banker's rounding and produce wrong invoice totals.",
        "at-0002": "Convert line prices with to_money Wrap line unit prices with ledgerly.money.to_money before arithmetic, and seed sums with ZERO from ledgerly.money, as line_total and invoice_total do.",
        "at-0003": "Raise BillingError with stable snake_case codes Reject invalid billing input by raising `BillingError` from `ledgerly.errors` with a snake_case code such as `invalid_state`, `invalid_quantity` or `negative_amount`, matching the existing `issue_invoice` pattern.",
        "at-0004": "Exclude bool when validating integer quantities When validating integer quantities, reject `bool` explicitly (`isinstance(quantity, bool)`) since `True`/`False` are ints in Python."
      }
    }
  },
